import{_ as e,j as a}from"./entry.8918adec.js";const t={},d=a('<h1 data-v-e2d1f66d>FAQ</h1><div class="faqBox" data-v-e2d1f66d><h2 data-v-e2d1f66d>General Questions</h2><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What is Cal Animage?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Cal Animage is an association of anime clubs that began in 1989, when its first club, Cal Animage Alpha, was founded in UC Berkeley. In following years, other clubs were founded at colleges such as UC San Diego and UC Irvine. These early anime clubs followed a Greek-letter naming tradition, each new club representing another “chapter” of Cal Animage.</p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>While most clubs no longer display this traditional naming system, these anime clubs have remained as part of Cal Animage to this day. Whether your club is new or long-standing, anime clubs of all kinds are welcome to become part of the Cal Animage Network!</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What does the Cal Animage Network do?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Shortly put, we are here to help you <b data-v-e2d1f66d>connect and collaborate.</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>We want to connect fellow anime clubs together under a common umbrella so that we can share and cooperate with one another. We help anime clubbers exchange ideas, share club materials, and offer expertise on how to better run our clubs and grow our communities.</p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Do you need resources for your clubs? Need some ideas for your club meetings? No idea how to run a maid cafe? Curious what your neighboring anime clubs are up to? Distance should not be an obstacle for helping other anime clubbers out. So let&#39;s head into this together.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>I&#39;m not a member of any club in Animage. Can I join one, or attend their meetings?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Each club has their own rules on club membership and who can attend their meetings. You will need to reach out to them on your own and adhere to their boundaries. Campus-based clubs will often only allow students from their own campus.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What is a Network Staffer? How can I become one?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Network staffers are individuals that have been on-boarded to help run the Network. We generally try to recruit from those that we know, or those that have a good history in an Animage club. You may apply through our Discord server.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Can my organization still affiliate or collaborate with the Network if it is not an anime club?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Yes! We are open to partnering and collaborating with organizations such as convention hosts, maid cafes, and sellers of art and merchandise. Please reach out to us on Discord or through email. </p></div><h2 data-v-e2d1f66d>Club-Related Questions</h2><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Why should my club be part of Cal Animage?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>We will be honest. The biggest reason why you should be part of Cal Animage is that it is nearly effortless. There are <b data-v-e2d1f66d>no required fees, no required work</b> from club officers, and <b data-v-e2d1f66d>no interference into your club affairs</b>.</p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Meanwhile in return, Animage clubs enjoy:</p><ul data-v-e2d1f66d><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Shared legacy as part of the world&#39;s oldest and largest association of anime clubs.</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Exclusive and easy access to up-to-date contact information for other Animage clubs.</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>A convenient platform for communication and collaborative projects with other Animage clubs.</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Permissions to send out club-related notifications (i.e. pings) to all other Animage clubs.</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>The right to be displayed on our website and Network map.</li></ul></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>How can my club join Cal Animage? What is (re)registration?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Registering or re-registering your club with the Cal Animage Network is easy! Clubs can apply and may be accepted anytime throughout the year.</p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>To (re)register, a club officer must complete a 5-minute application at <a href="/join" data-v-e2d1f66d>https://animage.moe/join</a></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>However, take note that <b data-v-e2d1f66d>November 1st</b> is the annual deadline for continuous re-registration. Clubs need to re-register and provide updated information every year in order to stay in the Network. If your club misses this deadline and re-registers late, its membership may be considered interrupted. </p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What is required before you can apply to join?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>To join the Network, your club must have...</p><ol data-v-e2d1f66d><li data-v-e2d1f66d>A primary in-person location (e.g. school campus, library, community center.)</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>A public web or social-media page.</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>An official original club logo (or mascot).</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Some rules for membership in your club.</li></ol></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Can my club join the Network if it is not exclusively an anime club? For example, if it were nominally an anime-gaming club, an or anime-comic club.</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>An element of Japanese animation will need to be a predominant feature of your club. Features such as having an anime mascot, or regularly watching anime, are good signs for qualification. We may determine on a case-by-case basis.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Can my anime club join if it is not campus-based (at a school)?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Yes. Being a school-based club is not a requirement.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Does my club need to be in California to join the Network?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Nope! We welcome clubs from all over the world. In-fact, some of our earliest clubs came from outside of California. We consider ourself a global network that happens to have roots in California, with its robust anime scene.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Can my anime club join if it is from a high school or middle school?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Unfortunately, our <a href="/docs" data-v-e2d1f66d>charter</a> requires that Animage clubs must be composed foremostly of “legal-aged adults.”</p></div><h2 data-v-e2d1f66d>Being Part of the Network</h2><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What is expected from clubs that are in the Network?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Clubs are expected to (1) complete a re-registration application at the beginning of each operational year and (2) uphold inclusive and cordial conduct. And that&#39;s it! All other involvement is completely voluntary.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>What authority will the Network have over my club?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>Cal Animage does not have authority to interfere in the internal affairs of any clubs.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>Who runs the Network?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>The Network is run by the <b data-v-e2d1f66d>Network Chairperson</b> and its <b data-v-e2d1f66d>Entrusted Clubs</b>, which are Animage clubs that have been specially entrusted to steer the Network. This “entrusted” distinction is a measure to ensure that Entrusted Clubs are stable and reputable enough to steer the Network in the long term.</p></div><div class="question" data-v-e2d1f66d><p data-v-e2d1f66d><b data-v-e2d1f66d>How can a club become an Entrusted Club?</b></p><p data-v-e2d1f66d>The <a href="/docs" data-v-e2d1f66d>charter</a> dictates that for a club to become entrusted, it must:</p><ul data-v-e2d1f66d><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Be distinguishably active (to similar levels of current Entrusted Clubs)</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Be recommended for entrustment by one current entrusted club</li><li data-v-e2d1f66d>Currently be in the Network for approximately at least 2 consecutive years, OR be a former entrusted club of at least 4 consecutive years, OR be among the original Cal Animage clubs founded in California from 1989 to 1994.</li></ul></div></div>',2);function o(i,n){return d}const s=e(t,[["render",o],["__scopeId","data-v-e2d1f66d"]]);export{s as default};
